{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-163822" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a plane lamina of mass $6\\,\\text{kg}.$ If the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass is $12.6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ what is the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis parallel to the first passing through a point on the lamina at a distance of $1.2\\,\\text{m}$ from its center of mass?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163822" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe distance between the lines is $d=1.2\\,\\text{m}.$ Then, applying the parallel axis theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & =12.6+(1.2)^{2}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =12.6+8.64 \\\\  & =21.24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $21.24\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163822" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-163822" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163822" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "14.84\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "16.25\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "21.24\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "24.32\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "28.21\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163822" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "21.24\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a plane lamina of mass $0.8\\,\\text{kg}$ and center of mass $(3,1),$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. If the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass is $2\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ what is the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis parallel to the first passing through the point $(1,-1)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe distance between the line through the center of mass $(3,1)$ and the line through the point $(1,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{(3-1)^{2}+(1-(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, applying the parallel axis theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & =2+(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}\\cdot 0.8 \\\\  & =2+6.4 \\\\  & =8.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $8.4\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-163827" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163827" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10.1\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "12.3\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "6.8\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "8.4\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "9.6\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163827" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8.4\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163820" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a plane lamina of mass $4\\,\\text{kg}.$ If the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass is $1.75\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ what is the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis parallel to the first passing through a point on the lamina at a distance of $45\\,\\text{cm}$ from its center of mass?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163820" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe distance between the lines is $d=45\\,\\text{cm}=0.45\\,\\text{m}.$ Then, applying the parallel axis theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & =1.75+(0.45)^{2}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =1.75+0.81 \\\\  & =2.56.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $2.56\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163820" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-163820" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163820" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1.45\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "1.5\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "1.75\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "2.25\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "2.56\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163820" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2.56\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a plane lamina of mass $8\\,\\text{kg}$ and center of mass $(4,1),$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. If the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass is $3.2\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ what is the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis parallel to the first passing through the point $(2,-1)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe distance between the line through the center of mass $(4,1)$ and the line through the point $(2,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{(2-4)^{2}+(-1-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, applying the parallel axis theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & =3.2+(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =3.2+64 \\\\  & =67.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $67.2\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-163829" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163829" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "52.3\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "56.4\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "64.2\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "67.2\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "72.5\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163829" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "67.2\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a plane lamina of mass $1\\,\\text{kg}.$ If the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass is $0.8\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ what is the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis parallel to the first passing through a point on the lamina at a distance of $1.5\\,\\text{m}$ from its center of mass?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe distance between the lines is $d=1.5\\,\\text{m}.$ Then, applying the parallel axis theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & =0.8+(1.5)^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0.8+2.25 \\\\  & =3.05.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $3.05\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-163824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1.52\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "2.25\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "2.55\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "3.05\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] ["math" "3.24\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3.05\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A rectangular plate of mass $\\frac{4}{5}\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-2\\le y\\le 2},$\nwhere $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 4=8\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{(\\frac{4}{5})}{8}=\\frac{1}{10}\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid:\n\n$$\n(\\overset{¯}{x},\\overset{¯}{y})=(\\frac{-1+1}{2},\\frac{-2+2}{2})=(0,0)\n$$\n\nSince the center of mass is at the origin, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\frac{1}{10}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=-2}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}4{x}^{2}+\\frac{16}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}{[\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{16}{3}x]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(\\frac{8}{3}+\\frac{32}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(\\frac{40}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}+(\\sqrt{2})^{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{8}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{44}{15}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-163172" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163172" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{14}{5}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{16}{5}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{44}{15}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{49}{15}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163172" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{44}{15}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}$\nand has mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x,$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters.\nGiven that the center of mass is at $(2,1),$ find the moment of inertia about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{3}\\cdot y{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =9\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass $(2,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}((x-\\overset{¯}{x})^{2}+(y-\\overset{¯}{y})^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}((x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}((x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2})2x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2x(x-2)^{2}+2x(y-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[2x(x-2)^{2}y+\\frac{2}{3}x(y-1)^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4x(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{4}{3}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}+16x+\\frac{4}{3}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}+\\frac{52}{3}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{4}-\\frac{16}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{26}{3}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =81-144+78-0 \\\\  & =15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =15+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})}^{2}\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =15+4 \\\\  & =19\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-164147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "19\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{16}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{25}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "19\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A rectangular plate of mass $\\frac{6}{5}\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-3\\le y\\le 3},$\nwhere $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 6=12\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{(\\frac{6}{5})}{12}=\\frac{1}{10}\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid:\n\n$$\n(\\overset{¯}{x},\\overset{¯}{y})=(\\frac{-1+1}{2},\\frac{-3+3}{2})=(0,0)\n$$\n\nSince the center of mass is at the origin, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\frac{1}{10}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=-3}^{y=3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}6{x}^{2}+18\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}{[2{x}^{3}+18x]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(4+36) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot 40 \\\\  & =4\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =4+(\\sqrt{5})^{2}\\cdot \\frac{6}{5} \\\\  & =4+6 \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-164139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "7\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A rectangular plate of mass $\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2},$\nwhere $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters.\nFind the moment of inertia of the plate about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 2=4\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{(\\frac{3}{2})}{4}=\\frac{3}{8}\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid:\n\n$$\n(\\overset{¯}{x},\\overset{¯}{y})=(\\frac{-1+1}{2},\\frac{0+2}{2})=(0,1)\n$$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}((x-\\overset{¯}{x})^{2}+(y-\\overset{¯}{y})^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}+3(y-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[3{x}^{2}y+(y-1)^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}6{x}^{2}+2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{[2{x}^{3}+2x]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(2+2-(-2-2)) \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =1+{(\\sqrt{6})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =1+9 \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-164142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{15}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{21}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A rectangular plate of mass $3\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1},$\nwhere $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=4\\cdot 2=8\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{3}{8}\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid:\n\n$$\n(\\overset{¯}{x},\\overset{¯}{y})=(\\frac{-2+2}{2},\\frac{-1+1}{2})=(0,0)\n$$\n\nSince the center of mass is at the origin, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{[{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=-1}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}2{x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{2}{3}x]}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}(\\frac{32}{3}+\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}(\\frac{40}{3}) \\\\  & =5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =5+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =5+\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-164140" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164140" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{15}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{21}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{23}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164140" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{23}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the moment of inertia of a circular plate that occupies the region of an annulus $D$ centered at $O$ with inner radius $1\\,\\text{m},$ outer radius $3\\,\\text{m},$ and mass density \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}},\n$$\n\n measured in $\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},$ about a line perpendicular to the ring passing through a point $2\\,\\text{m}$ from its center.\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n\\int {t}^{2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t=({t}^{2}-2t+2){e}^{t}+C\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nSince the mass density is symmetric in $x$ and $y,$ the center of mass is at $(0,0).$ The mass density function, in polar coordinates, is given by \n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{{e}^{r}}{r}.\n$$\n\nNext, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{e}^{r}}{r}\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{e}^{r}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={e}^{r}{|}_{1}^{3}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =({e}^{3}-e)\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =2\\pi ({e}^{3}-e)\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{e}^{r}}{r}\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{r}^{2}{e}^{r}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =({r}^{2}-2r+2){e}^{r}{|}_{1}^{3}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =(5{e}^{3}-e)\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =2\\pi (5{e}^{3}-e)\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $2\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =2\\pi (5{e}^{3}-e)+{2}^{2}\\cdot 2\\pi ({e}^{3}-e) \\\\  & =2\\pi (9{e}^{3}-5e)\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-163819" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163819" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\pi (5{e}^{3}-3e)\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "2\\pi (9{e}^{3}-5e)\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "4\\pi (3{e}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "4\\pi {e}^{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "6\\pi e\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163819" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\pi (9{e}^{3}-5e)\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the moment of inertia of a circular plate that occupies the region of an annulus $D$ centered at $O$ with inner radius $1\\,\\text{m},$ outer radius $\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m},$ and mass density $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{|xy|}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},$ measured in $\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},$ about a line perpendicular to the ring passing through a point $3\\,\\text{m}$ from its center." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nSince the mass density is symmetric in $x$ and $y,$ the center of mass is at $(0,0).$ The mass density function, in polar coordinates, is given by \n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{|r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta |}{{r}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{2}|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|.\n$$\n\nNext, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2}|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}r\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{r}^{2}{|}_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2-1)\\cdot [-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2}|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}{|}_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(4-1)\\cdot [-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $3\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}+{3}^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}+9 \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-164409" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164409" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{21}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{25}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{31}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164409" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{21}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A circular plate of mass $8\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region of a disk $D$ of radius $4\\,\\text{m}$ centered at the origin.\nFind the moment of inertia of the plate about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $0.5\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 4,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe area of the circular plate $D$ is $A=\\pi \\cdot {4}^{2}=16\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{8}{16\\pi }=\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid $(0,0).$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}{|}_{0}^{4}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\cdot 64\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =64\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $0.5\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =64+{0.5}^{2}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =64+2 \\\\  & =66\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-163815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "55\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "59\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "62\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "66\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "68\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "66\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A circular plate of mass $2\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region of a disk $D$ of radius $2\\,\\text{m}$ centered at the origin.\nFind the moment of inertia of the plate about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $4\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe area of the circular plate $D$ is $A=\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}=4\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{2}{4\\pi }=\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid $(0,0).$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}{|}_{0}^{2}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\cdot 4\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =4\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $4\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =4+{4}^{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4+32 \\\\  & =36\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-163213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "24\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "28\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "32\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "36\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "40\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-163213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "36\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-38587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the moment of inertia of a circular plate that occupies the region of a disk $D$ of radius $\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m}$ with mass density $\\lambda (x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2},$ measured in $\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},$ about a line perpendicular to the disk passing through a point on the circumference." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-38587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nSince the mass density is symmetric in $x$ and $y,$ its center of mass is at $(0,0).$ The mass density function, in polar coordinates, is given by $\\lambda (r,\\theta )={r}^{2}.$\n\nNext, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{2}\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =2\\pi \\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{2}\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line passing through a point on the circumference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}+{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}+4\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{20\\pi }{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-38587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-38587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-38587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "6\\pi "] ["math" "8\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{11\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{17\\pi }{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{20\\pi }{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-38587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{20\\pi }{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164132" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A circular plate of mass $3\\,\\text{kg}$ with uniform mass density occupies the region of a disk $D$ of radius $2\\,\\text{m}$ and is centered at the origin.\nGiven that the moment of inertia of the plate about a line $l$ perpendicular to the plate is $15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ find the distance of the line $l$ from the center of mass of $D.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164132" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe area of the circular plate $D$ is $A=\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}=4\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{3}{4\\pi }\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid $(0,0).$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{2}\\cdot \\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4\\pi }\\cdot 4\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem and solving for $d,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\ 15 & =6+3{d}^{2} \\\\ 3{d}^{2} & =9 \\\\ {d}^{2} & =3 \\\\ d & =\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164132" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-164132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\,\\text{m}"] ["math" "3\\,\\text{m}"] ["math" "6\\,\\text{m}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{m}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164149" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}$\nand has mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=4xy,$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. The moment of inertia of the plate about a line $l$ perpendicular to the plate is $\\frac{16}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nGiven that the center of mass of the plate is at $(2,\\frac{2}{3}),$ find the distance of the line $l$ from the center of mass." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164149" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =9\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass $(2,\\frac{2}{3})$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}((x-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}+(y-\\overset{―}{y})^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}((x-2)^{2}+{(y-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}((x-2)^{2}+{(y-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2})\\cdot 4xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x(x-2)^{2}y+x{y}^{3}-\\frac{4}{3}x{y}^{2}+\\frac{4}{9}xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{2}x(x-2)^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}x{y}^{4}-\\frac{4}{9}x{y}^{3}+\\frac{2}{9}x{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{2}x(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}x-\\frac{4}{9}x+\\frac{2}{9}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+\\frac{73}{36}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{[\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{4}-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{73}{72}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{81}{8}-18+\\frac{73}{8}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{5}{4} \\\\  & =5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem and solving for $d,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\ \\frac{16}{3} & =5+9{d}^{2} \\\\ 9{d}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ {d}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{27} \\\\ d & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ d & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{9}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164149" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-164149" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164149" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4\\,\\text{m}"] ["math" "6\\,\\text{m}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\,\\text{m}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{9}\\,\\text{m}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{m}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164149" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{9}\\,\\text{m}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina of mass $6\\,\\text{kg}$ about the perpendicular line passing through its center of mass is $4\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nIf the moment of inertia of the same lamina about another perpendicular line is $7\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ find the distance between the two lines." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nApplying the parallel axis theorem and solving for $d,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\ 7 & =4+6{d}^{2} \\\\ 6{d}^{2} & =3 \\\\ {d}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ d & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance between the two axes is $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,m.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-164128" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164128" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1\\,m"] ["math" "2\\,m"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\,m"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,m"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}\\,m"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164128" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,m"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-38584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina of mass $0.5\\,\\text{kg}$ about the perpendicular line passing through its center of mass is $0.2\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nIf the moment of inertia of the same lamina about another perpendicular line is $0.25\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ find the distance between the two lines. Round your final answer to two decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-38584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nApplying the parallel axis theorem and solving for $d,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\ 0.25 & =0.2+0.5{d}^{2} \\\\ 0.5{d}^{2} & =0.05 \\\\ {d}^{2} & =0.1 \\\\ d & =0.316\\,22….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance between the two axes is $0.32\\,m,$ rounded to two decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-38584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-38584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-38584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.05\\,m"] ["math" "0.1\\,m"] ["math" "0.25\\,m"] ["math" "0.32\\,m"] ["math" "0.64\\,m"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-38584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.32\\,m"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina of mass $3\\,\\text{kg}$ about the perpendicular line passing through its center of mass is $5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nIf the moment of inertia of the same lamina about another perpendicular line is $\\frac{35}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ find the distance between the two lines." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nApplying the parallel axis theorem and solving for $d,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\ \\frac{35}{4} & =5+3{d}^{2} \\\\ 3{d}^{2} & =\\frac{15}{4} \\\\ {d}^{2} & =\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ d & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance between the two axes is $\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\,m.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9fb33a0f002e6ca5e0224d293fed55e352d44efbe013dbe3bbea07bad1c388e"} {"question" "q-164130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4\\,m"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{4}\\,m"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\,m"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\,m"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}\\,m"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "q-164130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\,m"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/state.json" "file_sha256" "9d21c8dbe06e1bd35a40a491d5327a9347369547afe663b99ec50f6c16c7c353"} {"question" "e-11778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a plane lamina of mass $2\\,\\textrm{kg}$ and center of mass $(0,1),$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. If the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass is $2.5\\,\\textrm{kg}\\cdot\\textrm{m}^2,$ what is the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis parallel to the first passing through the point $(2,1)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/example-11778.json" "file_sha256" "611be318e11e35e1b4175d8c4c9acc5811c1aa1b1eb3a8c910f7382ca6a584c5"} {"question" "e-11778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line $l_M$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to $l_M$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = I_M + d^2M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and $I_M$ and $I_l$ are the moments of inertia about the lines $l_M$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe distance between the line through the center of mass $(0,1)$ and the line through the point $(2,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{(2-0)^{2}+(1-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, applying the parallel axis theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & =2.5+{2}^{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.5+8 \\\\  & =10.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $10.5\\,\\mathrm{kg}\\cdot\\mathrm{m^2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/example-11778.json" "file_sha256" "611be318e11e35e1b4175d8c4c9acc5811c1aa1b1eb3a8c910f7382ca6a584c5"} {"question" "e-12494" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A rectangular plate of mass $3\\,\\textrm{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\le x \\le 2, \\: 0 \\le y \\le 4 \\big\\},$\nwhere $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters.\nFind the moment of inertia of the plate about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $1\\,\\textrm{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/example-12494.json" "file_sha256" "027cf8142b134a3b84c45be9844847f0e5ed27c5ebe1f868f6e7279ce3bd4349"} {"question" "e-12494" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line $l_M$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to $l_M$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = I_M + d^2M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and $I_M$ and $I_l$ are the moments of inertia about the lines $l_M$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $\\mathcal{A} = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8\\,\\textrm{m}^2.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = \\dfrac{M}{\\mathcal{A}} = \\dfrac{3}8\\,\\textrm{kg}/\\textrm{m}^2,\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid:\n\n$$\n\\left(\\bar{x},\\bar{y}\\right) = \\left( \\dfrac{0+2}2, \\dfrac{0+4}2 \\right) = (1,2)\n$$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}((x-\\overset{¯}{x})^{2}+(y-\\overset{¯}{y})^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{3}{8}((x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}3(x-1)^{2}+3(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[3(x-1)^{2}y+(y-2)^{3}]_{y=0}^{y=4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}12(x-1)^{2}+16\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{[4(x-1)^{3}+16x]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(4+32-(-4+0)) \\\\  & =5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $1\\,\\textrm{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =5+{1}^{2}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =5+3 \\\\  & =8\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/example-12494.json" "file_sha256" "027cf8142b134a3b84c45be9844847f0e5ed27c5ebe1f868f6e7279ce3bd4349"} {"question" "e-11779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the moment of inertia of a circular plate that occupies the region of a disk $D$ of radius $1\\,\\textrm{m}$ with mass density $\\lambda(x, y) =2(x^2+y^2),$ measured in $\\textrm{kg}/\\textrm{m}^2,$ about a line perpendicular to the disk passing through a point on the circumference." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/example-11779.json" "file_sha256" "18b20378484c5a87add85c17947ccc353ffebc66eaaacdc3f7c4b6eb8904e015"} {"question" "e-11779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line $l_M$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to $l_M$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = I_M + d^2M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and $I_M$ and $I_l$ are the moments of inertia about the lines $l_M$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (r,\\theta) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq r \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq \\theta \\lt 2\\pi \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nSince the mass density is symmetric in $x$ and $y,$ $D$'s center of mass is at $(0,0).$ The mass density function, in polar coordinates, is given by $\\lambda(r,\\theta) = 2r^2.$\n\nNext, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{r}^{2}\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{r}^{4}{|}_{0}^{1}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =\\pi \\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{r}^{2}\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{r}^{6}{|}_{0}^{1}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line passing through a point on the circumference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+{1}^{2}\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/example-11779.json" "file_sha256" "18b20378484c5a87add85c17947ccc353ffebc66eaaacdc3f7c4b6eb8904e015"} {"question" "e-12493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A circular plate of mass $2 \\, \\textrm{kg}$ with uniform mass density occupies the region of a disk $D$ of radius $4 \\, \\textrm{m}$ and is centered at the origin.\nGiven that the moment of inertia of the plate about a line $l$ perpendicular to the plate is $24 \\, \\textrm{kg} \\cdot \\textrm{m}^2,$ find the distance of the line $l$ from the center of mass of $D.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/example-12493.json" "file_sha256" "2ad7c1b64a1b5ec1e4c3aaa5f139503c9ea6fac76bf69d36df9265d0c080c609"} {"question" "e-12493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line $l_M$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to $l_M$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = I_M + d^2M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and $I_M$ and $I_l$ are the moments of inertia about the lines $l_M$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (r,\\theta) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq r \\leq 4, \\: 0 \\leq \\theta \\lt 2\\pi \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nThe area of the circular plate $D$ is $\\mathcal{A} = \\pi \\cdot 4^2 = 16\\pi\\,\\textrm{m}^2.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda(r,\\theta) = \\dfrac{M}{\\mathcal{A}} = \\dfrac{2}{16\\pi} = \\dfrac{1}{8\\pi}\\,\\textrm{kg}/\\textrm{m}^2,\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid $(0,0).$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{4}\\cdot \\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8\\pi }\\cdot 64\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =16\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem and solving for $d,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\ 24 & =16+2{d}^{2} \\\\ 2{d}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {d}^{2} & =4 \\\\ d & =2\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/example-12493.json" "file_sha256" "2ad7c1b64a1b5ec1e4c3aaa5f139503c9ea6fac76bf69d36df9265d0c080c609"} {"question" "q-163172" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{44}{15}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071382/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "3d2051ddde0deea71223331ba3241e59c67947c6b38bccd731883f03f0f2d281" "reviewer_session" "01a11908-fa8d-7c61-8e03-c1185d0b9506" "rationale" "The rectangle has mass 4/5, side lengths 2 and 4, and centroid at the origin. Its central perpendicular moment is (4/5)(2²+4²)/12=4/3. The parallel axis theorem gives I=4/3+(√2)²(4/5)=44/15 kg·m². Original option 4 and the worked solution agree, and saved grading reports Correct. This is a derived judgment; the stored key differs only in unit typography." "bindings" {"problem" "9e45ead13d6967e0333b0ad270f26e638c4d593e2210d861e09c54f12faac4ea" "worked_solution" "492a4bbbdd5653f3183625696d72618273e05d33d3a5dfdf0b35798b60a24d04" "original_field" "10d790653abd462e3ee5f645710e24fb0cdd37d7470c3dff38063e220f0fdd42" "reviewed_field" "4dae15435dacbe3c7dc17b884084bf221790ef409c04eb493665ea458048cd31" "raw_widget" "c4c7654fd301f721a1f4